{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Python 3 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Python 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport sys\nfrom math import factorial as fact_func\n\ndef solve():\n    read = sys.stdin.readline\n    n, mod = map(int, read().split())\n    if n == 1:\n        print(0)\n        return\n\n    lst = [1]\n    ans = 0\n    i = 2\n    while i <= n:\n        len_lst = len(lst)\n        n_len = (i - 1) * i // 2 + 1\n        nz = [0] * n_len\n        d = [0] * (len_lst + 1)\n        for idx in range(len_lst - 1, -1, -1):\n            d[idx] = (d[idx + 1] + lst[idx]) % mod\n\n        for nz_idx in range(n_len):\n            L = max(0, nz_idx + 1 - i)\n            R = min(len_lst - 1, nz_idx)\n            nz[nz_idx] = (d[L] - d[R + 1]) % mod\n\n        e = [0] * (len(d) + 1)\n        f = [0] * (len(d) + 1)\n        for pos in range(len(d)):\n            e[pos + 1] = (e[pos] + d[pos]) % mod\n            f[pos + 1] = (f[pos] - pos * d[pos]) % mod\n\n        temp = 0\n        start = max(0, len_lst - i)\n        for j in range(start, len_lst - 2):\n            L = j + 2\n            temp = (temp + ((e[len_lst] - e[L]) * (i + 1 + j) + (f[len_lst] - f[L])) * lst[j]) % mod\n        for j in range(len_lst - i):\n            L = j + 2\n            R2 = i + j\n            temp = (temp + ((e[R2 + 1] - e[L]) * (i + 1 + j) + (f[R2 + 1] - f[L])) * lst[j]) % mod\n\n        ans = (ans + temp * (fact_func(n) // fact_func(n - (n - i)))) % mod\n        lst = nz\n        i += 1\n\n    print(ans % mod)\n\nsolve()\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.io.BufferedReader;\nimport java.io.InputStreamReader;\nimport java.util.StringTokenizer;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {\n        solve();\n    }\n\n    static void solve() throws Exception {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        StringTokenizer st = new StringTokenizer(br.readLine());\n        int n = Integer.parseInt(st.nextToken());\n        int mod = Integer.parseInt(st.nextToken());\n\n        if (n == 1) {\n            System.out.println(0);\n            return;\n        }\n\n        // precompute prodRatio[i] = product from i+1 to n modulo mod\n        long[] prodRatio = new long[n + 1];\n        prodRatio[n] = 1;\n        for (int i = n - 1; i >= 1; i--) {\n            prodRatio[i] = (prodRatio[i + 1] * (i + 1)) % mod;\n        }\n\n        int[] lst = new int[]{1};\n        long ans = 0;\n        int i = 2;\n\n        while (i <= n) {\n            int lenLst = lst.length;\n            int nLen = (i - 1) * i / 2 + 1;\n            int[] nz = new int[nLen];\n\n            long[] d = new long[lenLst + 1];\n            for (int idx = lenLst - 1; idx >= 0; idx--) {\n                d[idx] = (d[idx + 1] + lst[idx]) % mod;\n            }\n\n            for (int nzIdx = 0; nzIdx < nLen; nzIdx++) {\n                int L = Math.max(0, nzIdx + 1 - i);\n                int R = Math.min(lenLst - 1, nzIdx);\n                long val = (d[L] - d[R + 1]) % mod;\n                if (val < 0) val += mod;\n                nz[nzIdx] = (int) val;\n            }\n\n            long[] e = new long[lenLst + 2];\n            long[] f = new long[lenLst + 2];\n            for (int pos = 0; pos < lenLst + 1; pos++) {\n                e[pos + 1] = (e[pos] + d[pos]) % mod;\n                f[pos + 1] = (f[pos] - (long) pos * d[pos]) % mod;\n                if (f[pos + 1] < 0) f[pos + 1] += mod;\n            }\n\n            long temp = 0;\n            int start = Math.max(0, lenLst - i);\n            for (int j = start; j < lenLst - 2; j++) {\n                int L = j + 2;\n                long term1 = (e[lenLst] - e[L]) % mod;\n                if (term1 < 0) term1 += mod;\n                long term2 = (f[lenLst] - f[L]) % mod;\n                if (term2 < 0) term2 += mod;\n                long add = (term1 * (i + 1 + j) + term2) % mod;\n                add = (add * lst[j]) % mod;\n                temp = (temp + add) % mod;\n            }\n\n            for (int j = 0; j < lenLst - i; j++) {\n                int L = j + 2;\n                int R2 = i + j;\n                long term1 = (e[R2 + 1] - e[L]) % mod;\n                if (term1 < 0) term1 += mod;\n                long term2 = (f[R2 + 1] - f[L]) % mod;\n                if (term2 < 0) term2 += mod;\n                long add = (term1 * (i + 1 + j) + term2) % mod;\n                add = (add * lst[j]) % mod;\n                temp = (temp + add) % mod;\n            }\n\n            ans = (ans + temp * prodRatio[i]) % mod;\n            lst = nz;\n            i++;\n        }\n\n        System.out.println(ans % mod);\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-1.8358061424805783e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -5.376194530981593e-05, -0.0004167880106251687, 0.0, -0.0024756519123911858, -0.16022643446922302, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -0.0005529781919904053, -5.960462772236497e-07, -5.364403477869928e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -0.00033742457162588835, 